# `SELECT a, b` after a pipe is a plain column list, so `project` is certain.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | SELECT a, b | take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..25
  PIPELINE@0..24
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    PROJECT_OP@4..15
      IDENT@4..10 "SELECT"
      WHITESPACE@10..11 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@11..12
        NAME_REF@11..12
          IDENT@11..12 "a"
      COMMA@12..13 ","
      WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@14..15
        NAME_REF@14..15
          IDENT@14..15 "b"
    WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
    PIPE@16..17 "|"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    TAKE_OP@18..24
      IDENT@18..22 "take"
      WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
      LITERAL@23..24
        LONG@23..24 "1"
  WHITESPACE@24..25 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `SELECT` is not an operator
  --> query:1:5
  |
1 | t | SELECT a, b | take 1
  |     ^^^^^^
  |
  = help: choose or compute columns with `project`: `project a, b`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    t | project a, b | take 1
which parses without errors
